nds complicated tech, but difficulty communicating, egocentric, not willing to further education.\n\nCandidate A: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, leadership, but regarded as show-off, not open to new ideas.\n\nWe need to start discussion, maybe pick candidate with balanced strengths and fewer concerns. Candidate B has strong stress handling and conscientiousness, but interpersonal issues (nasty remarks) and weak memory for numbers (important for numbers). Candidate C has good decision making and calm, but communication issues and egocentric. Candidate D has problem solving and responsibility, but hot temper and know-it-all. Candidate A has anticipation and leadership but show-off and not open.\n\nWhich is best? Probably Candidate B's stress handling and conscientiousness are crucial, but interpersonal issues are serious for crew cooperation. Candidate C's communication issues also serious. Candidate D's hot temper also serious. Candidate A's show-off and not open to new ideas also concerning.\n\nMaybe none are perfect, but we need to start with a candidate and open discussion. Could recommend Candidate B but note concerns, ask others about crew cooperation evidence.\n\nThus first contribution: I propose Candidate B as provisional recommendation, citing strengths and concerns, and ask others for more info on interpersonal behavior.\n\nWe must include METADATA_JSON vote.\n\nProceed."}
